    {
      "id": "jTBhaW_Jixz2WCSJgfAmb",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -12585.321542577169,
      "y": 1977.8341745642829,
      "width": 283.5291748046875,
      "height": 35,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "CmP183T5y3rndnVgd7YFz"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bCc",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1653665864,
      "version": 409,
      "versionNonce": 1091160136,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788957880467,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What is quantization",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What is quantization",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "otwFjyTmz8f3MuomgLdhn",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -12946.821542577169,
      "y": 2037.3341745642829,
      "width": 1026.778076171875,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "CmP183T5y3rndnVgd7YFz"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bCd",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1385932616,
      "version": 689,
      "versionNonce": 473530184,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788957880467,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Quantization is a model compression technique that converts the weights and activations within an LLM\nfrom a high-precision data representation to a lower-precision data representation\n\n                            data type with more info --> data type with less info",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Quantization is a model compression technique that converts the weights and activations within an LLM from a high-precision data representation to a lower-precision data representation\n\n                            data type with more info --> data type with less info",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "YkDHpQYfj2X2QwiCE1TQa",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -12895.750541643522,
      "y": 3683.0670616734023,
      "width": 1026.778076171875,
      "height": 500,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "h6I1aOuilEoGTySvoW0NT"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bCe",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2117566024,
      "version": 1368,
      "versionNonce": 106583624,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788957880467,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Consider a concrete deployment where you want to serve a 13B LLM (e.g. Meta’s Llama 2 13B) on AWS.\n\nAWS’s g5.2xlarge instance has one NVIDIA A10G GPU with 24 GB of VRAM. AWS has published an on-\ndemand example price of $1.212/hour.\n\n                                          1.212 × 24 × 30 = $872.64/month\n\nOur model in full precision (FP32) need approximately:\n\n                                                  13B × 4bytes = 52 GB\n\nBut our GPU has only 24 GB :(\n\nSo we quantize to a lower precision (FP32 → INT8) so that each parameter requires less bytes.\n\nLet's say we quantize so that each parameter now need 1byte:\n\n                                                   13B × 1bytes = 13 GB\n\nNow the model can realistically fit amnd run faster.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Consider a concrete deployment where you want to serve a 13B LLM (e.g. Meta’s Llama 2 13B) on AWS.\n\nAWS’s g5.2xlarge instance has one NVIDIA A10G GPU with 24 GB of VRAM. AWS has published an on-demand example price of $1.212/hour.\n\n                                          1.212 × 24 × 30 = $872.64/month\n\nOur model in full precision (FP32) need approximately:\n\n                                                  13B × 4bytes = 52 GB\n\nBut our GPU has only 24 GB :(\n\nSo we quantize to a lower precision (FP32 → INT8) so that each parameter requires less bytes.\n\nLet's say we quantize so that each parameter now need 1byte:\n\n                                                   13B × 1bytes = 13 GB\n\nNow the model can realistically fit amnd run faster.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "yzBqBY9jPsp1WWrSOT6cx",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -12705.959424293264,
      "y": 3617.2337283400702,
      "width": 569.6903076171875,
      "height": 35,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "h6I1aOuilEoGTySvoW0NT"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bCf",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 373323080,
      "version": 723,
      "versionNonce": 1145589064,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788957880467,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Why using quantization -> $$$ and speed",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Why using quantization -> $$$ and speed",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "oVLetHDVhvx72etLGpGVw",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -12457.269694642446,
      "y": 6353.8444060591855,
      "width": 142.8006134033203,
      "height": 35,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "z1cGqbZ3_Q5-Bx8AHJXDj"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bCj",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1364693320,
      "version": 1321,
      "versionNonce": 817064264,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788957880467,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Calibration",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Calibration",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "k8UHN99kqVvCj0PkmReP_",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -12781.886134461782,
      "y": 6408.8444060591855,
      "width": 1026.778076171875,
      "height": 800,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "z1cGqbZ3_Q5-Bx8AHJXDj"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bCk",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1374038088,
      "version": 2875,
      "versionNonce": 134676552,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788957880467,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Calibration is the process of finding alpha and beta. \n\nA simple approach would be taking the minimum ancd maximum values in the model weights.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe problem is that very sensitive to outliers: there might be gaps between the alpha and the central\nvalues, which leads to wasting a lot of space in the quintized  space. \n\nWe have to make most of the use of tehe few bits we have!\n\nTo minimze this waste we could ignore the outliers.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe trade off is that we are loosing accuracy because all the outliers to the left and right will be\nclamped to q_min and q_max.\n\nThe final goal is to have the two distributinos to be as similar as possible. i.e. only way to minimize this\nis trying different therholds and measure the difference between the input and output distribution.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Calibration is the process of finding alpha and beta. \n\nA simple approach would be taking the minimum ancd maximum values in the model weights.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe problem is that very sensitive to outliers: there might be gaps between the alpha and the central values, which leads to wasting a lot of space in the quintized  space. \n\nWe have to make most of the use of tehe few bits we have!\n\nTo minimze this waste we could ignore the outliers.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe trade off is that we are loosing accuracy because all the outliers to the left and right will be clamped to q_min and q_max.\n\nThe final goal is to have the two distributinos to be as similar as possible. i.e. only way to minimize this is trying different therholds and measure the difference between the input and output distribution.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
